                    briefing_text_r1:       `The RFP asks for a generic <strong>leadership program for 180 managers</strong>, with a fixed R$4.2M budget and a board offsite in five months. But the discovery call revealed a <strong>stalling operational transformation</strong>: middle managers are disengaged, change is being resisted, and two safety incidents trace back to weak frontline leadership. Proença's method is <em>diagnosis before design</em> — separate the stated request from the underlying business challenge, name it in the CHRO's language, and identify the metrics her <strong>board</strong> will judge. Then decide how hard to challenge and re-contract the brief without losing the client.`,
